    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_95a8310e2e23f68eb94f02ecabfed5f5deca5fa51a1f0c0fefba3839a061e922",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across continuous joint, mixed, and discrete universality, the independence burden is represented at the level where simultaneous steering can fail: coefficient orthogonality or full matrix rank supplies separate directions for several functions, rational independence of the combined logarithmic frequencies supplies torus coordinates for mixed families, and discrete sampling adjoins the clock frequency 2pi/h, whose resonances may require deleting affected Euler factors. Functional identities and non-dense joint orbits show the complementary obstruction.",
