    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f8cdd383ce477b746905c83f1f87ef28da5342f2bc1a19f8b28634380c58f297",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The survey's ordinary-zeta and Hurwitz constructions expose a bounded representational contrast: finite Euler products steered through prime phases establish density only for nonvanishing targets, whereas shifted-integer frequencies, or a rational Hurwitz reduction to a jointly universal linear combination, support approximation of arbitrary holomorphic targets. The latter enlarged target class permits a zero-bearing local model, after which Rouche transfers its zero to the source function.",
